OL,3,GNEWSAFarmer says hosting 4G mast is a
OL,4,A'nightmare' as fees cost him thousands
OL,5,
OL,6,FA farmer says hosting 4G masts on his
OL,7,Fland has become a "nightmare" after the
OL,8,Frent he receives was halved, and it
OL,9,Fcost him #5,000 in fees.
OL,11,FAlan Watson, 68, from Llanbadarn Fynydd
OL,12,Fin Powys, has had a mast on his land
OL,13,Ffor more than 20 years, but claims
OL,14,Ffarmers are being "bullied" into
OL,15,Faccepting worse terms due to legal
OL,16,Fchanges between telecoms operators and
OL,17,Flandowners.
OL,19,FThe Farmers' Union of Wales (FUW) said
OL,20,Fit was concerned a cut in rent would
OL,21,Fput people off putting up masts,
OL,22,Faffecting connectivity in rural Wales.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,432,430,260,140,0,100
